      "writtenOn": "2023-07-25T16:44:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It might make sense to explicitly align the struct members with `@align` decorations (similarly to the Metal codegen adds members for padding). Since we\u0027re using std140 layout in both uniform and storage address spaces, there may be situations in which the SSBO alignment doesn\u0027t match std140 but WGSL doesn\u0027t complain because storage address-space alignment isn\u0027t as strict as uniform.\n\nThis particular test case should be OK (I believe `inputData` will be implicitly aligned to 16 bytes, according to the \"Internal Layout of Values\" https://www.w3.org/TR/WGSL/#internal-value-layout) but there might be situations in which that does\u0027t happen.",
      "revId": "22bd9536f114d8452272e7dab2d1ba4697a82443",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82aa889e_428c427a",
        "filename": "tests/sksl/shared/StorageBuffer.wgsl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-25T16:53:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, I\u0027ve already got a TODO to use MemoryLayout here, so I\u0027ll also add in the @aligns when I do that.\n\nI notice that our MemoryLayout class differentiates between `k140`, `kWGSLUniform` and `kWGSLStorage`. I should be using `k140` exclusively?",
      "parentUuid": "4f2386d2_0f0a7689",
      "revId": "22bd9536f114d8452272e7dab2d1ba4697a82443",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b8ad9b3_8cf64cab",
        "filename": "tests/sksl/shared/StorageBuffer.wgsl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-25T16:59:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e OK, I\u0027ve already got a TODO to use MemoryLayout here, so I\u0027ll also add in the @aligns when I do that.\n\u003e \n\nsgtm\n\n\u003e I notice that our MemoryLayout class differentiates between `k140`, `kWGSLUniform` and `kWGSLStorage`. I should be using `k140` exclusively?\n\nFor now I\u0027d say it\u0027s safer to use k140 since that\u0027s what Ganesh and Graphite use. \"WGSL Uniform\" and \"WGSL Storage\" alignments are slightly more relaxed compared to std140/std430 when it comes to matrices, e.g. mat2x2 has the same alignment as \"vec2, vec2\" rather than an array (tint does this conversion to provide a more packed layout), which we may want to consider taking advantage of in the future.",
      "parentUuid": "82aa889e_428c427a",
      "revId": "22bd9536f114d8452272e7dab2d1ba4697a82443",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
